{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Behold, etc.</b> The meaning: fire, the camp of the enemy — like \"For a fire went forth from Heshbon\" (Numbers 21:28)." "<b>To warm them.</b> A verb from the doubled [i.e., piel] binyan, and it is [a form] with a missing [root letter], on the pattern of לשכב את בת יעקב (Genesis 34:7). The meaning: they shall die, and no remnant shall remain to them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviated וגו' as 'etc.'; the comment is terse and the syntax of the gloss is compressed, rendered hyper-literally.", 1 "Read שלם as indicating a form with a dropped/assimilated root letter (i.e., חסר), following the comparison to לשכב which lacks a vav; alternatively שלם could mean 'complete' but the parallel with Genesis 34:7 favors the missing-letter reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:29.630708246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}